<%# Compact user row for the followers / following lists (and, via
    `blocks/index`, the blocked-users list). Locals: user, and an OPTIONAL
    `remove_path` (Slice C, gap 2). When `remove_path` is nil (the following /
    blocks / other-user-followers callers) the row renders exactly as it always
    has — a bare profile `link_to`. When present (only the owner's own followers
    page passes it) the row gains a trailing "Remove follower" pill: the outer
    element becomes a div carrying dom_id(user, :follower_row) so the
    remove_follower Turbo Stream can drop the row in place, the profile link takes
    `flex-1` inside it, and the DELETE button_to is a SIBLING of that link (never
    nested — a form inside an <a> is invalid HTML). The outline pill class literal
    is copied verbatim from `_follow_button`'s `:card` `outline_classes`.

    DESIGN SYSTEM (Slice 9, Task 4.4) —
    docs/design-system/components/social/UserRow.prompt.md: "40px avatar, medium name,
    faint light-grey @handle; hovers to `--color-gray-50`. Rows sit directly on white
    with a bottom border, not on separate cards." The name, the handle and the
    no-card-per-row shape were already right. Three things were not:

    - The avatar now goes through `ui/_avatar` at `row` (40px — the size exists in
      AVATAR_SIZES for this row and nothing else). `image_tag user.photo` raises on a
      blank photo, so a single photoless follower 500'd the whole followers page.
    - `border-b` carried no colour. Tailwind's reset leaves border-color at
      `currentColor`, and the base layer paints an `<a>` with `--fg-link` — so the
      separator rendered in brand indigo, a 1px blue rule between every row. It is the
      design system's `#f3f4f6` hairline, same as `ui/_divider`.
    - The hover fill was `hover:bg-neutral-<N>` off Tailwind's own `neutral` ramp, NOT
      Hoojah's `neutral` stance — a genuinely confusing collision, since a `*-neutral`
      utility means pink everywhere else in this app. The design system asks for
      `gray-50`, so that is what this row now says. (The old class name is spelled with
      a placeholder above on purpose: Tailwind reads these files as text with no
      ERB-comment awareness, so writing a dead utility in prose keeps generating a rule
      for it — the exact trap Task 4.2's review had to unpick.)

    A row is NOT a `ui/_card`: the list is one white surface with hairlines through it,
    and giving each row a shadow would grow the edges that `ui/_divider`'s header
    describes. The `shadow` lives on the list wrapper in each of the three callers. %>
<% remove_path = local_assigns[:remove_path] %>
<% if remove_path %>
  <div id="<%= dom_id(user, :follower_row) %>"
       class="flex items-center gap-3 p-3 bg-white border-b border-gray-100 hover:bg-gray-50">
    <%= link_to profile_path(user.username), class: "flex items-center gap-3 flex-1" do %>
      <%= render "ui/avatar", user: user, size: :row %>
      <div class="flex flex-col">
        <span class="font-medium"><%= user.full_name %></span>
        <span class="text-sm text-light-grey">@<%= user.username %></span>
      </div>
    <% end %>
    <%= button_to "Remove", remove_path, method: :delete,
          form: {data: {turbo_confirm: "Remove @#{user.username} from your followers?"}},
          class: "px-4 py-1 text-sm rounded-full border border-primary text-primary bg-card" %>
  </div>
<% else # nil remove_path: bytes IDENTICAL to the pre-Slice-C row (kept at column 0) %>
<%= link_to profile_path(user.username),
      class: "flex items-center gap-3 p-3 bg-white border-b border-gray-100 hover:bg-gray-50" do %>
  <%= render "ui/avatar", user: user, size: :row %>
  <div class="flex flex-col">
    <span class="font-medium"><%= user.full_name %></span>
    <span class="text-sm text-light-grey">@<%= user.username %></span>
  </div>
<% end %>
<% end %>
